"stem":146,"icon":147},"Journal and deception","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fjournal","5.security\u002F5.journal","i-lucide-book-lock",{"title":149,"path":150,"stem":151,"icon":152},"Compliance and posture","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fcompliance","5.security\u002F6.compliance","i-lucide-scale",{"title":154,"path":155,"stem":156,"icon":109},"SIEM export","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fsiem-export","5.security\u002F7.siem-export",{"title":158,"path":159,"stem":160,"icon":43},"Wazuh and Suricata","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fwazuh-suricata","5.security\u002F8.wazuh-suricata",{"title":162,"icon":163,"path":164,"stem":165,"children":166,"page":54},"Reference","i-lucide-book-marked","\u002Freference","6.reference",[167,172,177,182,187],{"title":168,"path":169,"stem":170,"icon":171},"Agent protocol","\u002Freference\u002Fprotocol","6.reference\u002F1.protocol","i-lucide-arrow-left-right",{"title":173,"path":174,"stem":175,"icon":176},"UI API","\u002Freference\u002Fui-api","6.reference\u002F2.ui-api","i-lucide-braces",{"title":178,"path":179,"stem":180,"icon":181},"Metric storage","\u002Freference\u002Fmetric-storage","6.reference\u002F3.metric-storage","i-lucide-database",{"title":183,"path":184,"stem":185,"icon":186},"Performance","\u002Freference\u002Fperformance","6.reference\u002F4.performance","i-lucide-gauge",{"title":188,"path":189,"stem":190,"icon":191},"Development","\u002Freference\u002Fdevelopment","6.reference\u002F5.development","i-lucide-code",{"id":193,"title":111,"body":194,"description":499,"extension":500,"links":501,"meta":502,"navigation":503,"path":112,"seo":504,"stem":113,"__hash__":505},"docs_en\u002F4.alerts\u002F4.incidents.md",{"type":195,"value":196,"toc":483},"minimark",[197,222,228,233,236,251,263,267,274,306,317,325,329,332,357,362,369,373,403,406,410,420,431,435,442,446,469,473],[198,199,200,201,205,206,210,211,210,214,217,218,221],"p",{},"A ",[202,203,204],"strong",{},"Wolf Incident"," groups the events of one rule for one group (a site, bench, host or label). It\nis ",[207,208,209],"code",{},"Open",", then ",[207,212,213],{},"Acknowledged",[207,215,216],{},"Resolved",". Rules with ",[202,219,220],{},"Auto Resolve"," close it when the\ncondition clears; a person can acknowledge or resolve it at any time, from the Wolf UI, Desk or a\nsigned link in the alert.",[223,224],"screenshot",{"alt":225,"caption":226,"name":227},"A resolved incident in the Wolf UI","A resolved incident: timeline with the deployment, the events, comments and status changes.","incident-resolved",[229,230,232],"h2",{"id":231},"the-timeline","The timeline",[198,234,235],{},"The incident's timeline interleaves its events with comments, assignments and status changes: who\nacknowledged or resolved it (from Version history), and auto-resolves (from the incident's own\nfields).",[198,237,238,241,242,245,246,250],{},[202,239,240],{},"Evidence"," is what the incident's rule matched: the events of an event rule, both events of a\nsequence rule, and for a metric rule its summary and the events behind the metric (the 502\nresponses of ",[207,243,244],{},"http_502","). Evidence is what the event count, Merge, Split and the proposed\n",[247,248,249],"a",{"href":86},"response actions"," work on.",[198,252,253,254,257,258,262],{},"The timeline also shows every other event of the incident's scope (site, bench, host) in its window,\nwhatever the source, as ",[202,255,256],{},"context",", and the deployment that preceded it. Sharing a site, bench or\nhost alone never makes an event evidence: a 502 on a site does not belong to the site's ",[259,260,261],"em",{},"Server\nScript can run new code"," incident. When the incident took events from other scopes (by\nIP or user, or through a sequence rule), it shows the deployments and health events of those scopes\ntoo: a Suricata alert on the database host comes with that host's deployment and failed crons, not\nthe Error Logs of every site it serves. Each user sees only the scopes they may read.",[229,264,266],{"id":265},"grouping-by-ip-or-user","Grouping by IP or user",[198,268,269,270,273],{},"A security event joins the open incident that holds an event naming the same IP or user, seen\nwithin ",[202,271,272],{},"Entity Correlation Minutes"," (60), whatever its source, host, bench or site. A Suricata scan\non one host, a Wazuh SSH alert on another and a web probe on a site, all from one address, read as\none incident.",[275,276,277,285,300,303],"ul",{},[278,279,280,281,284],"li",{},"Only a public remote address (",[207,282,283],{},"payload.ip",") counts. A server's own address, private, loopback and\ndocumentation ranges would tie unrelated attacks together.",[278,286,287,288,291,292,295,296,299],{},"A user ties events only when it is an e-mail address (",[207,289,290],{},"root"," on two hosts or ",[207,293,294],{},"Administrator"," on\ntwo sites are not one person), and not from failed logins or ",[207,297,298],{},"sudo"," failures, whose user the\nattacker chose.",[278,301,302],{},"Only incidents started in the last 24 hours take events by entity, so a scanner coming back every\nhour does not keep one incident growing.",[278,304,305],{},"A rule's evidence is its own: when a rule fires on events another incident took by IP, they move\nto the rule's incident.",[198,307,308,309,312,313,316],{},"Both settings are in ",[202,310,311],{},"Wolf Settings → Correlation",". Untick ",[202,314,315],{},"Group Incidents by IP or User"," (on by\ndefault) and events become evidence only of the rules that match them.",[198,318,319,320,324],{},"Each event says who raised it: the Wolf agent, the Wolf site, Suricata or Wazuh. An event that is\nthe ",[247,321,323],{"href":322},"\u002Fsecurity\u002Fwazuh-suricata#both-one-finding-two-sources","same finding"," as another source's says\n\"same finding as …\" and links to that row when it is on the page.",[229,326,328],{"id":327},"working-an-incident","Working an incident",[198,330,331],{},"Wolf Managers can:",[275,333,334,344,350],{},[278,335,336,339,340,343],{},[202,337,338],{},"Assign to me",", or set ",[202,341,342],{},"Assigned To",". Frappe's assignment runs (ToDo, sidebar, notification to\nthe assignee), and the sidebar's own assign and unassign keep the field in step.",[278,345,346,349],{},[202,347,348],{},"Add comment"," on the timeline. Wolf Users can comment too.",[278,351,352,353,356],{},"Take a ",[247,354,355],{"href":86},"response action"," on a security incident.",[358,359,361],"h3",{"id":360},"manual-incidents","Manual incidents",[198,363,364,365,368],{},"Create one in Desk, or use ",[202,366,367],{},"Open incident from this event"," on a Wolf Event. Manual incidents have\nno rule, so the rules engine never auto-resolves them.",[358,370,372],{"id":371},"merge-and-split","Merge and split",[275,374,375,393],{},[278,376,377,380,381,384,385,388,389,392],{},[202,378,379],{},"Merge into…"," (Desk: ",[202,382,383],{},"Actions","; Wolf UI: ",[202,386,387],{},"Merge…",") moves events and comments to the target\nand resolves the source with ",[202,390,391],{},"Merged Into"," set. If the source came from a rule, further\nbreaches of that rule feed the target instead of opening a duplicate.",[278,394,395,398,399,402],{},[202,396,397],{},"Split…"," moves the events you tick to a new incident (no rule, ",[202,400,401],{},"Split From"," set).",[198,404,405],{},"The Wolf UI's dialogs say what will move and what each incident becomes before you confirm.",[229,407,409],{"id":408},"postmortems","Postmortems",[198,411,412,415,416,419],{},[202,413,414],{},"Write postmortem"," on a resolved incident creates a ",[202,417,418],{},"Wolf Postmortem",":",[275,421,422,425,428],{},[278,423,424],{},"summary, impact (scope, duration, event count), root cause, lessons;",[278,426,427],{},"action items, each with an owner, a due date and a status;",[278,429,430],{},"a frozen, escaped snapshot of the timeline.",[229,432,434],{"id":433},"metrics","Metrics",[198,436,437,438,441],{},"The ",[202,439,440],{},"Wolf Incident Metrics"," script report gives incidents, MTTA (acknowledged − started) and MTTR\n(resolved − started): average, p50 and p90 in minutes, per site, bench, host, rule or severity, over\na date range. Merged incidents are left out, so an outage counts once.",[229,443,445],{"id":444},"regulatory-reporting","Regulatory reporting",[198,447,448,449,452,453,456,457,460,461,464,465,468],{},"Flag an incident as a ",[202,450,451],{},"Significant incident (NIS2 Art. 23)",", a ",[202,454,455],{},"Major ICT-related incident (DORA\nArt. 19)"," or a ",[202,458,459],{},"Personal data breach (GDPR Art. 33)"," to start its deadlines. They are shown on\nthe incident, and the ",[202,462,463],{},"Regulatory deadline"," preset alerts before each one. Wolf tracks dates only:\nit does not decide what is reportable and sends nothing to an authority. See\n",[247,466,467],{"href":150},"Compliance",".",[229,470,472],{"id":471},"public-status","Public status",[198,474,475,476,479,480,468],{},"Give an incident a ",[202,477,478],{},"Public Title"," to control how it appears on a ",[247,481,482],{"href":117},"status page",{"title":484,"searchDepth":485,"depth":486,"links":487},"",1,2,[488,489,490,495,496,497,498],{"id":231,"depth":486,"text":232},{"id":265,"depth":486,"text":266},{"id":327,"depth":486,"text":328,"children":491},[492,494],{"id":360,"depth":493,"text":361},3,{"id":371,"depth":493,"text":372},{"id":408,"depth":486,"text":409},{"id":433,"depth":486,"text":434},{"id":444,"depth":486,"text":445},{"id":471,"depth":486,"text":472},"Acknowledge, assign, merge, split and close incidents, and write the postmortem.","md",null,{},{"icon":114},{"title":111,"description":499},"fniF1Z7hKl4o_Gz4dUoECX21TDTXUHsr4geBVIiY30o",[507,509],{"title":106,"path":107,"stem":108,"description":508,"icon":109},"Send alerts to email, chat, push, SMS or PagerDuty, and set up each destination.",{"title":116,"path":117,"stem":118,"description":510,"icon":119},"Publish a public status page for a site, with no internal detail.",1794949747821]